      "targetText": "2. Identify the exact closed macro space and canonical onto isometryThe conditional projection equals the orthogonal projection onto H_P=lpMeas. Its range is H_P and it fixes every vector in H_P. The accepted actual range theorem identifies the SAME canonical M range with ran(P); restrict M to its range and use that equality to obtain the isometric equivalence e with inclusion i e=M. Ambient product measurability and completeness of the closed subspace are derived internally.HP=ranP=ranM,P|HP=IHP,e:L2(ν;R)≃HP,ie=M.Corresponding Lean step  have hPdef : P = HP.starProjection := rfl\n  have hPrange : P.toLinearMap.range = HP := by\n    change P.range = HP\n    rw [hPdef]\n    exact HP.range_starProjection\n  have hMR : M.toLinearMap.range = P.toLinearMap.range :=\n    (MacroscopicRange.actual_macro",
