      "targetText": "5. Transport the internally constructed positive real scalar rootThe shared real L² root theorem produces Γ≥0 with Γ²=I−T². Define Γ_P by the SAME e-conjugation. Adjoint conjugation preserves positivity; the star-algebra equivalence preserves multiplication, subtraction and identity, so Γ_P²=I_H_P−A² and agrees with the preceding typed Gram operator. No real CFC or root witness is a public premise.Γ≥0,Γ2=I−T2,ΓP=eΓe−1≥0,ΓP2=IHP−A2=B∗B.Corresponding Lean step  obtain ⟨Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hEnergy⟩ :=\n    AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareRoot.exists_positive_real_square_root\n      ν ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) hD\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  have hΓP : ΓP.IsPositive := by\n    simpa only [ΓP,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply,e.adjoint_eq_symm] u",
